 "v1_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from July to September 2026 (E-07), and since tariff rates did not change (E-02) and most disputed bills carry ACTUAL, non-estimated reads rather than ESTIMATED ones (1785 vs 1240, E-03), the surge is not explained by a tariff change or by field/AMI read-collection failure. The dominant supported mechanism is a billing-side defect in the import/calculation/validation step that turns accepted actual reads into wrong bills, driving the dispute increase (H-ACTUAL-READ-BILLING-DEFECT).",
