 "v2_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from July to September 2026, reaching 1260 tickets (E-07). The dominant supported mechanism: billing-import validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 and comparing raw register values directly against 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-13), misreads firmware v4.2 AMI meters (which report in 0.1 m3 units vs v3.x meters' m3 units, E-14) as ~10x true consumption, causing billing import to reject 1184 of 1240 valid, before-cutoff AMI reads as HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-12) and forcing estimate substitution that produces wrong/estimated bills, driving the ESTIMATED-dispute portion of the surge.",
